"""
Mango, sugarcane and chilli (user request, 11 Nov 2026): neither PlantVillage nor PlantSeg has them, so their diseases follow the
classes of the main public datasets for each crop. Only the class names are used (as aliases), no images.
  * Mango: MangoLeafBD (Ahmed et al. 2023, Mendeley Data 10.17632/hxsnvwty3r.1): anthracnose, bacterial canker, cutting weevil,
    die back, gall midge, powdery mildew, sooty mould (+ healthy).
  * Sugarcane: Sugarcane Leaf Disease Dataset (Daphal & Koli 2022, Mendeley Data 10.17632/9424skmnrk.1): mosaic, red rot, rust,
    yellow (+ healthy).
  * Chilli: "chili v2" (Roboflow Universe, CC BY 4.0): leaf curl, leaf spot, powdery mildew, whitefly (+ healthy, yellowish), and the
    Bangladesh chilli leaf set (Mendeley Data wzc6r6w5w5): anthracnose, cercospora leaf spot, leaf curl disease (+ fresh leaf).
    "yellowish" (unspecified yellowing) is not given a disease of its own.
Content notes as in plantseg_existing.py: general plant-pathology knowledge, not reviewed by a plant pathologist, no product or dose.
"""
